{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515670-has-anyone-played-masquerade-fully-as-requiem","id":1515670,"title":"Has anyone played Masquerade fully as Requiem?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-20T08:46:01-07:00","id":1515670,"title":"Has anyone played Masquerade fully as Requiem?","content":"I like the simplified dice system of Requiem, but I don't want to leave behind an ounce of the lore of Masquerade. I also don't want to lose any the <i>stuff </i>Masquerade has - Vicissitude, all 30+ Thaumaturgy paths, Mytherceria, etc.<br /> <br /> Has anyone attempted to convert Masquerade fully into Requiem? I know the Translation Guide is a start, but is it a feasible task to move all of Masquerade into the Requiem system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28045-watt-grego","name":"Watt Grego","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T09:26:35-07:00","id":1515672,"title":"","content":"Its very much a possible task. Mind you it will require time and energy but if you are determined to carry out and complete a project like this I see no reason as to why you couldn't do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T11:51:01-07:00","id":1515683,"title":"","content":"Aside from making rough plans to translate some of the base concepts of some clans into covenants (Insular vampire mages, Seers tapped into to an eldritch hivemind, Assassins for hire, Vampire families; etc...) nope. I like my two kindred as different from each other as I can make them (hell, I don't even have clans in my VtR games)<br /> <br /> But sure, you can translate.<br /> For most of the work, like disciplines, you can probably use the translation guide as a reference (with a little extra legwork, if you're using 2nd Edition). I haven't looked at <i>Sacrements &amp; Blasphemies</i> for a few years now, but that might help with the likes of Thaumaturgy and Necromancy and moving the rituals over.<br /> <br /> The problem with the lore side of things, imo, is that it's going to clash with blood potency. You can borrow from V5's generation+potency mashup, I guess, but I'd consider the generation and potency incompatible. Perhaps you could remove the restrictions and drawbacks and simply assign potency based on generation; though you can also keep them and have the legends of the methuselah's thirst being real, if you like.<br /> <br /> For example;<br /> Potency = Generation<br /> 10 = 4<br /> 9 = 5<br /> 7 = 6<br /> 6 = 7<br /> 5 = 8<br /> 4 = 9<br /> 3 = 10<br /> 2 = 11<br /> 1 = 12<br /> 0 = 13 (revenant drawbacks like sweating vitae all day not included)<br /> <br /> Thinbloods are going to be a little trickier to pull off, not sure what to do there. You could remove 4th gen from the chart and bump it up so that 13th are potency 1 and generations 14-16 are potency 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T12:23:32-07:00","id":1515684,"title":"","content":"I heard about attempt of use the two concepts like two different creatures, but I don't know anymore details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T21:04:19-07:00","id":1515716,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a quick translation of Masquerade\u2019s thirteen Clans, in this site\u2019s Requiem subforum. See the \u201cRequiem Homebrew Hub\u201d thread. Same thread also has disparate conversions of Masquerade Clans/Bloodlines as Requiem Bloodlines, mostly under 1e (nWoD) mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}